WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:04.840
We are about to begin a journey beyond ordinary
human understanding

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.200
Lost somewhere between immensity and eternity

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.680
Join me, as we explore: Our Amazing 
Debt

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:24.560
We are all made of star stuff -- and in America, we're all born more than 61
thousand dollars in debt

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:28.500
The collective debt we owe as a country now stands at 20 trillion dollars

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.300
A level of debt unfathomable to our contemptible
caveman ancestors

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.380
How can we comprehend the sheer magnitude of our national debt?

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.440
With our starship of imagination

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.600
This is the USS Dumbitdownforme

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.740
and it cost 12 billion dollars to construct

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:52.420
all financed through debt

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:55.469
We didn’t have the money to build it and
we didn’t want to raise taxes to pay for it

00:00:55.469 --> 00:00:57.170
but we really wanted it

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:02.430
So, like a fiscal wormhole, we’ve used debt
to puncture the reality of financial constraints

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:07.220
connecting what we want now to promises of paying even more money later

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:11.030
Let’s take a look inside and see what
20 Trillion dollars really means

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:16.140
20 trillion dollars isn’t just a lot of
money, it’s all of the money, and then some

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:21.520
If we could round up all the US currency in
existence - every dollar bill, every quarter, every penny

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:24.800
we'd still need another 18 Trillion dollars

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.940
All the gold that’s ever
been mined couldn’t even cover half of our debt

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:30.500
Yet our story doesn't end here

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.300
Like our ever-expanding universe

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.300
our debt is constantly growing larger

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:39.720
This year we'll pay more than 250 billion dollars on interest payments

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:43.100
not the debt, just the fee for borrowing money

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:47.140
Much as cosmic expansion will inevitably lead to the heat death of our own universe

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.600
the debt, too, is unsustainable

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:53.160
As nature seeks balance so too will our creditors

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:57.720
Will the government gut spending? Defund entitlements? Devalue our currency?

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.720
One day, perhaps in our lifetime

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:03.520
we will discover the answers and reach the limit of our amazing debt

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:08.300
But for now we can only behold the awesome force that binds all Americans

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:12.300
bewitching us with the fascinating possibility that maybe

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.300
just maybe

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.300
we're all f*cked

